{"content":[{"id":"3aa6be64","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"1db708cf","settings":{"__dynamic__":{"image":"[elementor-tag id=\"\" name=\"post-featured-image\" settings=\"%7B%22fallback%22%3A%7B%22url%22%3A%22%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22%22%2C%22size%22%3A%22%22%7D%7D\"]"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"theme-post-featured-image","elType":"widget"},{"id":"27d3241","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A drain backing up is one of the most frustrating plumbing problems homeowners face. Whether it\u2019s a slow sink, a clogged shower, or water coming back up where it shouldn\u2019t, it\u2019s usually a sign of a deeper issue.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The tricky part is that drain backups don\u2019t always happen all at once. Most start as small problems, like slow drainage, gurgling sounds, or occasional clogs, before turning into a full blockage.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At <\/span><b>Petitt Heating &amp; Cooling<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, we help homeowners across Springfield, Hendersonville, White House, and surrounding Middle Tennessee communities identify the cause of drain backups and fix them before they lead to bigger plumbing issues.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your drain is backing up, here\u2019s what could be causing it and what you should do next.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"68e898f8","settings":{"title":"Quick Answer: Why Is My Drain Backing Up?\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5ee98ce7","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drains usually back up due to blockages, pipe damage, or sewer line issues. Common causes include grease buildup, hair clogs, debris, tree root intrusion, or damaged pipes. Identifying the cause early helps prevent water damage and costly plumbing repairs.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"ac0756f","settings":{"title":"1. Drain Clogs from Everyday Buildup\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6f444358","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The most common cause of a drain backup is a simple clog.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Over time, materials build up inside pipes and restrict water flow.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common culprits include:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Grease and food debris (kitchen drains)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hair and soap residue (bathroom drains)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Paper products and waste (toilets)<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"72e3a5cb","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As buildup increases, water slows down and eventually has nowhere to go, causing a backup.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6509ab3d","settings":{"title":"What You Can Do:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"67436d16","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use a plunger or basic drain clearing methods<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Avoid pouring grease down the drain<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Clean drains regularly<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3050dda5","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If clogs keep coming back, the problem may be deeper in the line.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1b2ca778","settings":{"title":"2. Sewer Line Blockages\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"37af155e","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If multiple drains in your home are backing up at the same time, the issue is likely in your main sewer line.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is more serious than a single drain clog.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Signs of a sewer line problem:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Multiple drains backing up<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water coming up in tubs or floor drains<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Strong sewer odors<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Gurgling sounds in pipes<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7f2d625e","settings":{"title":"What To Do:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7762a310","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is not a DIY fix. Sewer line problems require <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/expert-plumbing-services-in-springfield-hendersonville-white-house-and-beyond\/\"><b>professional plumbing inspection and repair<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to prevent major damage.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5604becc","settings":{"title":"3. Pipe Damage or Deterioration\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"723ca5b0","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Older or damaged pipes can restrict flow and lead to frequent backups.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Over time, pipes can:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Corrode<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Crack<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Collapse<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Shift due to soil movement<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"57f467fd","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This reduces the space water has to flow through.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1e950384","settings":{"title":"What You Can Do:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"45aa97c6","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If backups are frequent or getting worse, a plumber can inspect your system and determine if repairs or replacement are needed.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"362dca69","settings":{"title":"4. Improper Items Flushed or Drained\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2a11c015","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many drain backups are caused by <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.southernliving.com\/things-never-put-down-drain-11852774\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">items that should never go down the drain.<\/span><\/a><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common problem items:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201cFlushable\u201d wipes<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Paper towels<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Grease or oil<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hygiene products<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Food scraps<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5f817ec5","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These materials don\u2019t break down easily and can create stubborn blockages.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"251ad652","settings":{"title":"Prevention Tip:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"25919192","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Only flush toilet paper and avoid disposing of grease or debris in drains.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4616f9d","settings":{"title":"5. Venting Issues in Your Plumbing System\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1053e690","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your plumbing system relies on proper venting to maintain airflow.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If vents are blocked, it can cause:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Slow drainage<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Gurgling sounds<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Intermittent backups<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3d55c6e1","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blocked vents prevent air from moving through the system, which affects how water flows.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2af73474","settings":{"title":"What to Do:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3625ac72","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Venting issues usually require professional diagnosis and correction.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"31a762d4","settings":{"title":"Why Drain Backups Get Worse Over Time\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1f90738b","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drain problems rarely fix themselves.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What starts as a slow drain can quickly turn into:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Full blockages<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water damage<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sewer backups<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Unsanitary conditions<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"ccf35bb","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The longer the issue is ignored, the <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.angi.com\/articles\/plumber-cost.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">more expensive<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> it becomes to fix.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2847fe1f","settings":{"title":"What You Can Safely Try (and When to Call a Plumber)\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"53a2a3f6","settings":{"title":"Safe DIY Steps:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"79e27387","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use a plunger<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Remove visible debris<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try basic drain cleaning methods<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Run hot water for grease buildup (kitchen only)<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"229026fc","settings":{"title":"Call a Professional If:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"38d260b0","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Multiple drains are backing up<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You notice sewage smells<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water is coming up from other drains<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Clogs keep returning<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You suspect a sewer line issue<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"54c6c63b","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Professional plumbing service can quickly identify the root cause and <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/spring-plumbing-maintenance-checklist\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">prevent further damage.<\/span><\/a><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"75cdd1fe","settings":{"title":"How Petitt Heating & Cooling Helps\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"53f0d253","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At Petitt Heating &amp; Cooling, we provide fast, reliable plumbing services to homeowners across Middle Tennessee.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our team helps with:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drain cleaning and clog removal<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sewer line inspections<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Leak detection and repair<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pipe repairs and replacements<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Preventive plumbing maintenance<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"76f1c353","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We focus on identifying the cause of the problem\u2014not just clearing the symptom.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5ef4bf10","settings":{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions About Drain Backups\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"20ec5d8d","settings":{"items":[{"item_title":"Why is my sink backing up but other drains are fine?","_id":"b1f25e5"},{"item_title":"Can a clogged drain fix itself?","_id":"1f42309"},{"item_title":"What are signs of a sewer line problem?","_id":"e9a76d0"},{"_id":"eeb3b14","item_title":"Is it safe to use chemical drain cleaners?"},{"_id":"913e57c","item_title":"How do plumbers fix drain backups?"}],"__globals__":{"title_typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=accent"}},"elements":[{"id":"34dd8ed5","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"22635538","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This usually indicates a localized clog in that specific drain rather than a main sewer line issue.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"2fceaafb","settings":{"_title":"item #2","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"483f53b1","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. Clogs typically worsen over time as more debris builds up inside the pipe.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"3fc11901","settings":{"_title":"item #3","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"561336e5","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Multiple drains backing up, sewage odors, gurgling pipes, and water coming up in unexpected places are common warning signs.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"57a83fdd","settings":{"_title":"Item #4"},"elements":[{"id":"3eb3f458","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Chemical cleaners can damage pipes and often don\u2019t fully resolve the issue. Repeated use may cause more harm than good.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"2a9dacfc","settings":{"_title":"Item #5"},"elements":[{"id":"2c11ca6d","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plumbers use tools like drain snakes, hydro jetting, and camera inspections to locate and remove blockages or repair damaged pipes.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true}],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"nested-accordion","elType":"widget"},{"id":"73969472","settings":{"title":"Don\u2019t Wait for a Small Backup to Become a Big Problem\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"567f2dfa","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A backed-up drain is more than just an inconvenience\u2014it\u2019s a warning sign that something isn\u2019t working correctly in your plumbing system.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Addressing the issue early can help you avoid water damage, costly repairs, and larger plumbing problems.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your drains are backing up, Petitt Heating &amp; Cooling is ready to help.<\/span><\/p><p><b>Call today or <\/b><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/contact-us\/request-an-appointment\/\"><b>schedule service online<\/b><\/a><b> to restore proper drainage and protect your home.<\/b><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"}],"settings":{"template":"default"},"metadata":{"ao_post_optimize":"a:6:{s:16:\"ao_post_optimize\";s:2:\"on\";s:19:\"ao_post_js_optimize\";s:2:\"on\";s:20:\"ao_post_css_optimize\";s:2:\"on\";s:12:\"ao_post_ccss\";s:2:\"on\";s:16:\"ao_post_lazyload\";s:2:\"on\";s:15:\"ao_post_preload\";s:0:\"\";}","et_enqueued_post_fonts":"a:3:{s:6:\"family\";a:1:{s:12:\"et-gf-oswald\";s:34:\"Oswald:200,300,regular,500,600,700\";}s:6:\"subset\";a:2:{i:0;s:5:\"latin\";i:1;s:9:\"latin-ext\";}s:9:\"cache_key\";s:73:\"{\"gph\":-1,\"divi\":\"4.27.4\",\"wp\":\"6.9\",\"enable_all_character_sets\":\"false\"}\";}"}}